  <!-- AGENTS.md topology approximation for read-only oracle experiments; NOT hardware calibrated.
Known: 34 channels, 8 dies/channel, 6 planes/die, 16 KiB NAND pages.
User hardware naming is channel->die->chip->plane; each user die has 1 chip and 6 planes.
MQSim grouping 1 chip/channel x 8 dies/chip is a topology adapter, not hardware nomenclature.
Uniform MQSim topology uses 272 dies / 1632 planes; actual device has 271 / 1626.
128 pages/block and 32 blocks/plane are SIMULATION capacity placeholders, not hardware values.
User corrected the read/write Block to 6408 pages x 16 KiB, not a physical hierarchy level.
Do not equate that Block with MQSim's physical NAND erase block; not encoded.
User-confirmed NAND technology: TLC.
User accepts remaining experiment defaults: PCIe, NAND transfer rate and latencies
remain upstream values; block geometry retains the adapter's capacity placeholders.
These accepted defaults are simulation assumptions, not hardware measurements.
Six-plane independent-cache/command behavior is not validated against the real NAND.
See ssd_agents_34ch_8die_6plane.README.md before interpreting results.
-->
